      "text": "About: In the Multiverse of Matter, thousands of parallel worlds exist, and most of them get through their darkest night. Wormwood is not one of them. It is a universe frozen at 1:23 a.m. on 26 April 1986, the night Chernobyl’s Reactor 4 failed, and its clocks will not move until someone sets things right. The only thing that can calm its core is the Prima Materia, a mythical substance said to rewrite matter itself. But a rogue scientist, once ignored when she warned of this very night, has stolen it and sealed it away. Time is running out in Wormwood, and it is now up to you. Operation Blackout is a high-stakes, timed puzzle chase where every answer you crack unlocks the next challenge. Four connected levels stand between your team and the final solution, and none of them can be skipped. There is no textbook shortcut here. You will have to think like an alchemist, a circuit designer, a signal engineer and a gene hunter, often within the same five minutes. The challenges draw on many branches of engineering, so you will need a team that can reason under pressure and stay calm while the clock counts down. One shared countdown of 90 minutes runs for the entire game, and wrong turns and hints cost you precious time, so only the fastest and most precise teams will make it to the end. Open to 2nd, 3rd and 4th-year students, this is an event for the curious, the competitive and anyone who loves a good mystery. So gather your team, trust each other and be ready for the moment the lights go out. Wormwood is waiting, and its clock has already started.",
